  "Question": "The general term is \\(a_n=4n−1\\). What is the common difference?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The coefficient of the linear term, 4, is the common difference.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the common-difference definition\n\nThe common difference is the change from any term to the next. For every positive integer \\(n\\),\n\\[\na_{n+1}-a_n=[4(n+1)-1]-(4n-1)=4.\n\\]\nThis difference is constant, so the common difference is \\(4\\).",
